# The bayan-core commit whose WebAssembly engine package bayan-web builds and serves (work package WEB-002).
# During Phase 0, before bayan-core publishes releases, the shells build core from a pinned commit (ADR-0002 §4); from the first
# release on, the web app consumes the published package instead, pinned exactly.
# scripts/engine-package.sh builds engine-package/ from this commit. Before that, scripts/check-engine-pin.sh refuses any commit that
# is not one of the commits of bayan-core's main branch, so only reviewed and merged engine code reaches the app, and any commit that
# reached main less than 24 hours before now or before the bayan-web commit that added the commit line below (at the earlier of its
# author and committer times; a later change to these comments does not count), as ADR-0017 rule 4 sets out for dependencies (its
# amendment of 2026-10-12 exempts this pin during Phase 0, but bayan-web keeps the 24 hours; AGENTS.md says why); it reads the history,
# so it refuses a shallow clone of bayan-web.
# `pnpm verify` fails if engine-package/ was built from another commit.
# Change it like a dependency: in its own pull request, saying what changed in bayan-core between the two commits.
